{
  "enabled": true,
  "name": "Dependency Security Checker",
  "description": "Monitors package.json and lock files for changes and automatically checks for security vulnerabilities, outdated dependencies, and suggests updates. Helps maintain a secure and up-to-date codebase.",
  "version": "1",
  "when": {
    "type": "fileEdited",
    "patterns": [
      "package.json",
      "pnpm-lock.yaml",
      "yarn.lock",
      "package-lock.json"
    ]
  },
  "then": {
    "type": "askAgent",
    "prompt": "Analyze the dependency changes in the package files and provide a security and maintenance report:\n\n1. **Security Vulnerabilities**: Check if any new or updated dependencies have known security issues\n2. **Outdated Dependencies**: Identify dependencies that are significantly behind their latest versions\n3. **Breaking Changes**: Warn about potential breaking changes in major version updates\n4. **Bundle Size Impact**: Assess if new dependencies significantly increase bundle size\n5. **Dependency Conflicts**: Check for potential version conflicts between dependencies\n6. **License Compatibility**: Verify that new dependencies have compatible licenses\n\nFor each finding:\n- Explain the potential risk or impact\n- Provide specific version recommendations\n- Suggest migration steps for major updates\n- Prioritize issues by severity (Critical/High/Medium/Low)\n\nConsider the project uses pnpm as the package manager and includes React, TypeScript, Vite, and Supabase dependencies."
  }
}